 "notes": {
  "went_wrong": "Camerupt caught the Earthquake intended for Marowak. Video confirms Clodsire used Earthquake, although the bot labeled the accepted throw Stone Edge after it tapped the second button. Back at one Pok\u00e9mon left, the tracker still thought Snorlax had 8 HP and sent 20 futile switch taps after the catch, interrupting Clodsire\u2019s fast taps. The Icy Wind shield at 58.2 s also reviewed poorly.",
  "tap_review": "476 fast taps, median 0.155 s. The near-faint retry guard paused at 69.5 s as buttons disappeared, then detected the accepted Mirror Coat and ran its minigame. Seven charged moves actually executed. On the late catch, Earthquake was tapped at 181.55 s, the recognition change was logged 0.21 s later, and Stone Edge was tapped at 181.92 s before the Earthquake animation was identified. No transport errors.",
  "switch_review": "Opening Araquanid and Snorlax switches confirmed in 0.52 and 0.92 s. The later Araquanid switch was interrupted by Bone Club, then confirmed 0.69 s after the retry. At 165.4 s the bot recognized Clodsire, but the team count fell to one while the tracker kept fainted Snorlax alive. Three initial switch taps and twenty retries were directed at Snorlax in total, including the successful earlier switch and two retries; the late futile switches were one initial tap at 190.69 s, an unsuccessful attempt at 197.51 s, and eighteen \u201cagain\u201d taps.",
  "shield_review": "The model preferred no shield on Bone Club and Shadow Ball early. At 58.2 s the engine declined the shield, but the matchup override protected against a possible lethal Shadow Ball. The move was Icy Wind. The hindsight replay preferred saving the shield, 66% vs 11% in simulation (31 to 79 percentage point loss interval). The Rock Tomb shield comparison was inconclusive.",
  "record_correction": "The structured play-by-play uses video-confirmed Earthquake. The raw log still shows the incorrect Stone Edge label. The catch was excluded from automated decision scoring because the simulated view was already on Camerupt by the time the move began. Video confirms it was a catch. The earlier Icy Wind shield and the late switch attempts are separate issues."
 },
